= Choosing our enemies

In our media and campaign materials, who should we consider as our main opponents?

[? if enemies != 0 : Previously, we had considered the [+ enemies +] as our prior enemies. Is a change of direction necessary? ?]

- @confederates: Former Confederates, who caused the Civil War to protect slavery.
- @KKK: New Paramilitaries found in the south. 
- @imma: The new immigrants, particularly Irish and Germans.
- @bourgeois: The elites and wealthy in society
- @easy_discard

@confederates
on-arrival: enemies = "confederates"; radical_strength += 5 if radical_split = 0; middle_class_rad += 2 if radical_split = 1; freemen_rad += 2 if radical_split = 1; moderate_strength += 5; conservative_dissent += 5; workers_dem -= 2; middle_class_rep -= 2; freemen_rep -= 2; liberal_dissent += 2

Aiming our focus at the former Confederates amongst our midst is popular among the entire party, although the <span style="color: #B5651D;">**Conservative Republicans**</span> are worried that we are too aggressive against a now defeated enemy.

@KKK
on-arrival: enemies = "KKK"; radical_strength += 5 if radical_split = 0; freemen_rad += 2 if radical_split = 1; radical_dissent -= 5; moderate_dissent += 5; rural_dem -= 3; unemployed_dem -= 3; liberal_strength += 2; liberal_dissent -= 1

[? if kkk_rise = 0 and year < 1867 : The southern paramilitary groups are still small and scattered, barely more than rumor in the northern press. Some in the party question whether they deserve to be called our enemy at all. ?][? if kkk_rise = 0 and year >= 1867 : The Klan and similar night-riding societies are still scattered, but reports of intimidation against freedmen are growing. Some in the party think we are naming a threat before it has fully arrived, others that we are naming it just in time. ?][? if kkk_rise = 1 and kkk_strength + whiteL_strength < 400 : The Klan has become a real menace across the South, and it is the greatest obstacle to our Black supporters. Naming it as our enemy is an easy sell. ?][? if kkk_rise = 1 and kkk_strength + whiteL_strength >= 400 : Paramilitary violence in the South has reached a scale that can no longer be ignored. Naming the Klan[? if whiteL_formed = 1 : and the White League ?] as our enemy is hardly controversial. ?][? if kkk_rise = 2 : The Klan has been broken as an organized force. Some argue we are fighting a battle already won, while others warn that its remnants[? if whiteL_formed = 1 : and the White League ?] are only waiting for us to look away. ?]

@imma
on-arrival: enemies = "immigrants"; conservative_strength += 5; immigrant_laborers_rep -= 5; workers_rep += 3; liberal_dissent += 3; liberal_strength -= 2

Despite having bigger priorities at the moment, we decide to go after the immigrants who pose to steal the jobs of the northern workers.

@bourgeois
on-arrival: enemies = "bourgeois"; workers_rep += 3; conservative_dissent += 8; workers_dem -= 3; workers_other -= 5; liberal_strength -= 3; liberal_dissent += 4

Our anti-bourgeois rhetoric is popular among the workers, but these ideas are fringe and may reduce funding from our patrons.
